DESC_START
# SP-B-X-006 — C5 Semantic drift refresh policy

**Tier**: M
**Prefer**: claude
**Class**: subscription-claude
**Authority required**: L3
**Blocked by**: nothing (independent)

#### Context (per design doc §C5 line 605-618)

Long contexts: model "remembers" iter-5 file content but iter-30 model thinks file is unchanged. Design line 617 prescribes "every N iterations, N=10, issue unsolicited `view` of the most-edited file".

#### Code AC

- [ ] **Survey first**: locate the runner-side Anthropic client. Candidate: `backend/agents/anthropic_native_client.py`. If different, document the actual module name in the AC PR.
- [ ] **Wire refresh injection** into that client: after every N user-message iterations, inject a synthetic `text_editor view` tool call on a target file.
- [ ] Policy config (env vars):
  - `OMNISIGHT_RUNNER_STALE_REFRESH_EVERY_N_ITER` (default 10)
  - `OMNISIGHT_RUNNER_STALE_REFRESH_STRATEGY` (default `most-edited`; alternatives: `random-touched`, `all-touched`)
  - `OMNISIGHT_RUNNER_STALE_REFRESH_MAX_TOKENS` (default 1000)
- [ ] **Strategy module**: `backend/agents/stale_refresh_strategy.py` exposes `pick_refresh_target(touched_files, strategy) -> str | None`.
- [ ] Transcript logging: every refresh emits `[stale-refresh-injected] view {file} at iter {N} (strategy={strategy})`.
- [ ] Cost gate: if estimated refresh cost > `OMNISIGHT_RUNNER_STALE_REFRESH_MAX_TOKENS`, skip with `[stale-refresh-skipped] cost-budget-exceeded`.

#### Test scope

- Unit: strategy picker (most-edited, random-touched, all-touched).
- Unit: cost-gate skip logic.
- Integration: synthetic long session → transcript contains refresh markers at iter 10/20/30.

#### Non-goals

- Do NOT add semantic-diff or hash check on refresh result.
- Do NOT change Anthropic API client outside the refresh-injection point.

#### Boundaries

