## OP-1074
SUMMARY: [SP-B-X-016] Add .runner-cwd-sentinel to _OUR_OWN_ARTIFACTS (OP-1060 follow-up)
STATUS: 承認済み
LABELS: adr:0035,agent:auto,area:backend,area:tests,class:subscription-codex,hot-fix,parent:SP-B-X-META,prefer:codex,priority:critical,schema:v0,scope:sprint-s12-g,scope:sprint-sp-b-x,ticket-id:sp-b-x-016,tier:S,type:feature
DESC_START
# SP-B-X-016 — Add .runner-cwd-sentinel to _OUR_OWN_ARTIFACTS (OP-1060 follow-up)

**Parent**: OP-1058 SP-B-X-META
**Hot-fix path**: operator-authorized B route — claude pushed Gerrit **#554** directly to develop on 2026-05-14 (this ticket is paper trail).

## Context

OP-1060 (SP-B-X-002a) added phase-snapshot stashing at FSM boundaries via `git stash push --include-untracked`. The exclusion set `_OUR_OWN_ARTIFACTS` at `backend/agents/runner_progress.py:146` covered `progress.txt` + `progress.txt.tmp` but omitted the OP-842 `.runner-cwd-sentinel` — even though the function's own docstring at line 164 cites the sentinel as analogous-shape fix. The omission caused:

1. Pickup writes `.runner-cwd-sentinel` (untracked)
2. `record_phase('picking_up')` → `take_phase_snapshot()` → `_worktree_dirty()` sees `?? .runner-cwd-sentinel` → returns True
3. `git stash push --include-untracked` removes the sentinel from working tree
4. Post-CLI sentinel-check fires `[runner-workspace-tampered]` → revert

Affected: OP-1069 (claude-2), OP-1071 (claude-2), OP-1070 (claude-1 AND codex). Both runner classes trip the bug (proven on OP-1070 codex revert at 02:07:51).

## Code AC

- [x] Add `.runner-cwd-sentinel` to `_OUR_OWN_ARTIFACTS` set (Gerrit #554)
- [ ] Merge #554 to develop
- [ ] Verify OP-1070 next pickup succeeds without tamper

## Boundaries

```yaml
loc_delta_max: 20
files_touched_max: 1
required_paths:
  - backend/agents/runner_progress.py
class: subscription-codex      # ad-hoc filed; commit already pushed
authority_required: L3
tag_type: story
schema_version: v0
external_systems: [gerrit]
external_side_effect: write
reversibility: reversible
```

## Disposition

- Gerrit change pushed by claude (ad-hoc) per operator's option-B directive
- Ticket filed AFTER commit for ledger completeness
- Once merged + OP-1070 closes, SP-B-X-META can close


DESC_END

## OP-1075
SUMMARY: [SP-B-X-017] Exclude progress.txt from ensure_change_ids dirty-check (OP-1060 follow-up #2)
STATUS: 承認済み
LABELS: adr:0035,agent:auto,area:backend,class:subscription-codex,hot-fix,parent:SP-B-X-META,prefer:codex,priority:critical,schema:v0,scope:sprint-s12-g,scope:sprint-sp-b-x,ticket-id:sp-b-x-017,tier:S,type:feature
DESC_START
# SP-B-X-017 — Exclude progress.txt from ensure_change_ids dirty-check (OP-1060 follow-up #2)

**Parent**: OP-1058 SP-B-X-META
**Hot-fix path**: operator-authorized B route — claude pushed Gerrit **#555** directly. Paper trail.

## Why this is the SECOND fix

SP-B-X-016 (Gerrit #554, OP-1074) fixed `runner_progress._OUR_OWN_ARTIFACTS` to exclude `.runner-cwd-sentinel`. That stopped the workspace-tampered revert path.

But the SAME bug exists in `jira_dispatch.ensure_change_ids()` (line 1039-1046) — a DIFFERENT post-AC dirty-check that previously only filtered the sentinel. OP-1060 didn't add `progress.txt` to that filter.

Observed on OP-1070:
- 02:39:06 picked up
- 02:46:29 AC verified ✓ (codex committed the work)
- 02:46:42 `[runner-dirty-worktree] CLI exited with 1 uncommitted path(s); First few: ['progress.txt']` → revert

## Fix

Renamed local filter to `_RUNNER_OWN_ARTIFACTS = {".runner-cwd-sentinel", "progress.txt", "progress.txt.tmp"}` and applied to both. Now both dirty-checks tolerate progress.txt.

## Code AC

- [x] `ensure_change_ids` excludes progress.txt + progress.txt.tmp (Gerrit #555)
- [ ] Merge #555
- [ ] OP-1070 succeeds on next pickup

## Boundaries

```yaml
loc_delta_max: 25
files_touched_max: 1
required_paths:
  - backend/agents/jira_dispatch.py
class: subscription-codex
authority_required: L3
tag_type: story
schema_version: v0
```

Sibling to SP-B-X-016 / OP-1074.


