## OP-1076
SUMMARY: [SP-B-X-018] Consolidate _RUNNER_OWN_ARTIFACTS + add dirty-check tests + evaluate .gitignore migration
STATUS: 公開済み
LABELS: adr:0035,agent:auto,area:backend,area:docs,area:tests,capability:enable=code_edit,capability:enable=gerrit_push,capability:enable=jira_update,capability:enable=run_lint,capability:enable=run_tests,class:subscription-codex,parent:SP-B-X-META,prefer:codex,priority:high,runner-blocked:waiting-OP-1074,schema:v0,scope:sprint-s12-g,scope:sprint-sp-b-x,tech-debt,ticket-id:sp-b-x-018,tier:S,type:feature
DESC_START
# SP-B-X-018 — Consolidate _RUNNER_OWN_ARTIFACTS + add dirty-check tests + evaluate .gitignore

**Parent**: OP-1058 SP-B-X-META
**Blocked by**: SP-B-X-016 (OP-1074) + SP-B-X-017 (OP-1075) — both hot-fixes must merge first

## Why this ticket

The two ad-hoc hot-fixes pushed 2026-05-14 (Gerrit #554 + #555) addressed the SP-B-X-002a side effects (workspace-tampered on `.runner-cwd-sentinel` and dirty-worktree on `progress.txt`) but left three code-quality debts behind:

### Debt 1 — Duplicated filter sets

The "runner-runtime files that should be invisible to dirty-checks" list now lives in TWO places:

```python
# backend/agents/runner_progress.py:146
_OUR_OWN_ARTIFACTS = frozenset({
    PROGRESS_FILENAME,                          # progress.txt
    PROGRESS_FILENAME + _PROGRESS_TMP_SUFFIX,   # progress.txt.tmp
    ".runner-cwd-sentinel",                      # ★ added by #554
})

# backend/agents/jira_dispatch.py:1044-ish (post-#555)
_RUNNER_OWN_ARTIFACTS = {
    ".runner-cwd-sentinel",
    "progress.txt",
    "progress.txt.tmp",
}
```

Adding a 4th runner-internal file in the future requires updating both. Refactor: single canonical constant exported from `runner_progress` (or a new `runner_artifacts.py` module), imported by both consumers.

### Debt 2 — No unit tests

Neither hot-fix added tests. A refactor of `ensure_change_ids` or `_worktree_dirty` could silently drop the filter and reintroduce the wedge. Required tests:

- `tests/test_ensure_change_ids_ignores_runner_artifacts.py`:
  - `test_ignores_runner_cwd_sentinel()` — write sentinel as untracked, call ensure_change_ids, assert no raise
  - `test_ignores_progress_txt()` — same for progress.txt
  - `test_ignores_progress_txt_tmp()` — same for .tmp
  - `test_still_raises_on_unrelated_dirty_file()` — write `foo.py` as dirty, assert WorktreeDirtyError raised
- `tests/test_runner_progress_dirty_filter.py`:
  - Equivalent suite for `_worktree_dirty()`

### Debt 3 — Evaluate `.gitignore` as the proper fix

OP-842 + OP-1060 + SP-B-X-016 + SP-B-X-017 are all "layered filter" fixes. The architecturally correct fix is to add these three files to repo-level `.gitignore` so `git status` itself excludes them — no per-callsite filter needed.

This ticket should:
- Document why `.gitignore` was not used (so future engineers can re-evaluate)
- IF `.gitignore` is decided to be the right move, this ticket converts: add to `.gitignore`, remove both filter sets, ensure no regression

## Code AC

- [ ] Single canonical constant `RUNNER_RUNTIME_ARTIFACTS` (or similar) exported from one module, used by both `runner_progress._worktree_dirty` and `jira_dispatch.ensure_change_ids`
- [ ] Both filter sites import the canonical constant (no duplication)
- [ ] Unit tests covering all 3 artifacts × 2 callsites (6 positive cases) + 2 negative cases (unrelated dirty file in each callsite)
- [ ] Decision in `docs/sop/runner-runtime-artifacts.md`: keep filter-based approach OR migrate to `.gitignore`. Reasoning documented.
- [ ] If `.gitignore` migration chosen: filter sets removed; full regression test pass

## Non-goals

- Do NOT introduce new runner-runtime files in this ticket (scope: only the existing 3)
- Do NOT change `ensure_change_ids` semantics beyond the filter consolidation
- Do NOT touch other dirty-checks in the codebase (those may have their own exclusion contracts)

