## §4. ADR-0035 skeleton (preview)

This is what SP-B-X-013 will produce. Included here so codex can validate the split is sensible.

```markdown
# ADR-0035: Runner FSM + Error Handling Contract

## Status
Adopted (2026-05-NN by sora + claude-bot + codex-bot)

## Supersedes
None. Codifies design at `docs/architecture/sdk-runner-sprint-b-error-handling.md`
(2026-05-09 / PS3 2026-05-10) which was implementation reference, not a binding ADR.

## Context
Runner pipeline (pickup → execute → push → transition) has lacked a binding FSM
+ invariant contract since Sprint B design (5/9). The 14 SP-B per-child tickets
shipped without elevating the cross-cutting contract to ADR. This caused 4
cross-cutting gaps (§C1, C3, C5, C8) to never get filed + §C4 to ship in
inverse-direction only (OP-1044). 2026-05-13's OP-1048 incident exercised exactly
the unsupported §C4 direction.

## Decision

### 1. Top-level FSM (binding)
(Verbatim from architecture doc §2 line 36-98)

### 2. Invariants I1-I6 (binding)
(Verbatim from architecture doc §2 line 99-110)

### 3. External system ordering (binding — §C4)
State-transition order is **Gerrit-push first, JIRA-transition second**. If JIRA
transition fails after Gerrit success, retry transition with deterministic
idempotency token of form `{ticket_key}:{operation_type}:{args_hash}` per §4 below.

### 4. Idempotency primitives (binding — §7)
Idempotency token = `f"{ticket_key}:{operation_type}:{args_hash}"`.
  - ticket_key: JIRA ticket key (e.g. "OP-1052")
  - operation_type: stable enum from `{pickup, transition, comment, assign, release}` (architecture §7 line 698-700)
  - args_hash: 12-char sha256 hex prefix of canonical-JSON input material; for transitions this is `{"target_status": <name>, "patchset": <change_number>}` (target_status encodes "under-review" / "approved" / etc. — operation_type stays "transition" regardless)

NO UUID fallback in code paths that finalize Gerrit-side success.

## Consequences
- All runner code must align with this FSM. SP-B-X-001..012 are the implementation tickets.
- `docs/architecture/sdk-runner-sprint-b-error-handling.md` is now implementation appendix.

## Rejected alternatives
- Promote whole 807-line architecture doc: too rigid; per-child catalogs change frequently.
- Keep as architecture-only: no binding contract → cross-cutting gaps recur (proven by 2026-05-13).
- Split FSM from invariants into two ADRs: false separation; invariants enforce the FSM.

## Relationship to other ADRs
- ADR-0023 (Foundation Rebuild) Phase 31.B: implements runner fix; aligned.
- ADR-0033 (Governance Engine): L1/L2/L3 authority hierarchy is honored by §C11 detection in SP-B-X-011.
- ADR-0034 (Override Review): override audit trail uses idempotency tokens per ADR-0035 §4.
```

---

## §5. Risk + rollback registry

| Risk | Trigger | Rollback |
|---|---|---|
| §C4 fix breaks existing finalization | SP-B-X-001 lands but `_finalize_under_review` regresses | Revert SP-B-X-001; bridge force-walk still rescues legacy path |
| Reaper false-positive (SP-B-X-002) | Reaper reaps still-live runner | `OMNISIGHT_RUNNER_REAPER_ENABLED=0` |
| TOCTOU reread storms JIRA REST (SP-B-X-004) | Every phase boundary fires extra JIRA fetch | Built-in rate-limit (60s per ticket); configurable |
| ADR-0035 split confuses future authors | Future runner work edits only architecture doc | ADR-0035 header includes pointer back; architecture doc inverts pointer to ADR |

