# SP-B-X-016 — Add .runner-cwd-sentinel to _OUR_OWN_ARTIFACTS (OP-1060 follow-up)

**Parent**: OP-1058 SP-B-X-META
**Hot-fix path**: operator-authorized B route — claude pushed Gerrit **#554** directly to develop on 2026-05-14 (this ticket is paper trail).

## Context

OP-1060 (SP-B-X-002a) added phase-snapshot stashing at FSM boundaries via `git stash push --include-untracked`. The exclusion set `_OUR_OWN_ARTIFACTS` at `backend/agents/runner_progress.py:146` covered `progress.txt` + `progress.txt.tmp` but omitted the OP-842 `.runner-cwd-sentinel` — even though the function's own docstring at line 164 cites the sentinel as analogous-shape fix. The omission caused:

1. Pickup writes `.runner-cwd-sentinel` (untracked)
2. `record_phase('picking_up')` → `take_phase_snapshot()` → `_worktree_dirty()` sees `?? .runner-cwd-sentinel` → returns True
3. `git stash push --include-untracked` removes the sentinel from working tree
4. Post-CLI sentinel-check fires `[runner-workspace-tampered]` → revert

Affected: OP-1069 (claude-2), OP-1071 (claude-2), OP-1070 (claude-1 AND codex). Both runner classes trip the bug (proven on OP-1070 codex revert at 02:07:51).

## Code AC

- [x] Add `.runner-cwd-sentinel` to `_OUR_OWN_ARTIFACTS` set (Gerrit #554)
- [ ] Merge #554 to develop
- [ ] Verify OP-1070 next pickup succeeds without tamper

